{"summary":"Full source ledger traced: every limitation of claims 1-15, all 26 reference numerals, and the specific structures, relationships, results, positions, connections, operating conditions and variants in draft/04 through draft/10 and in all six figure briefs trace to exact affirmative passages of input/disclosure.md (identical to the single USER passage in input/conversation.md). Title, applicant/inventor, "Not applicable" cross-reference and "Not applicable" government-support statement match input/brief.md, which was used only for those formalities.

Consistency checks that passed: (1) Section-line designation 3-3 is repeated identically in the source-view brief (figures/FIG-1.md:17, which also states the numeral 3 is a section designation and not a reference numeral), in the resulting view (figures/FIG-3.md:3), in the Brief Description (draft/07-drawings.md:5) and in the detailed description (draft/08-detailed-description.md:27). (2) The FIG. 1 arrow direction (both arrows pointing right off the vertical cutting-plane line on the topmost carriage centre line) is geometrically consistent with FIG. 3's stated "view's right being the axial side from which FIG. 1 is viewed." (3) The view-orientation chain closes: FIG. 4 viewed from the side opposite FIG. 1 with radially outward up correctly places second cam ring segment 24 at the left, first cam ring segment 22 at the right, and the handle leaning toward first frame half 10, which is the exact transform of the same-side orientation used in FIG. 1 and FIG. 6; the frame-wall interruption radially outside segment 24 is the same in FIG. 4 and FIG. 6. (4) The kinematics close: the wedge slant in FIG. 4 drives segment 24 clockwise as seen from FIG. 1/FIG. 2, and the FIG. 2 slot tilt converts clockwise ring rotation into inward follower travel; the ring drive face is deepest at its joint-nearest end and stops short of the parting line in both FIG. 2 and FIG. 4. (5) Slot positions in FIG. 2 match carriage positions in FIG. 1; the annular-guide opening direction matches between FIG. 3 and FIG. 5. (6) Every numeral used in a brief appears in draft/numerals.md, every tabled numeral is used in the description and appears in at least one figure, and no numeral carries two meanings. (7) No drafting note, placeholder, open question, instruction, unresolved alternative or internal comment remains in any draft file, and no shape-justifying sentence ("by way of example", "any closed outline", optional-shape embodiment) appears in the application text; all schematic hedges stay inside the figure briefs. (8) Claims contain no means-plus-function language, antecedent bases resolve (including "a pipe received in the frame" introduced in claim 1 and claim 10), three statutory classes are supported, and summary, description and claims use the same relationships and terms; the source's "complementary drive faces" is disambiguated consistently as "complementary coupling faces" (segment joints) versus "ring drive face" (wedge-engaged face), with no change of meaning.

One item does not clear the depiction-convention test: figures/FIG-1.md states the circumferential positions of the three jaw carriages and their allocation between the two frame halves as flat fact rather than as a schematic choice, while figures/FIG-2.md expressly flags the corresponding choice ("the positions and tilt of the three slots") as shown schematically. The disclosure says only that the carriages are "distributed around the closed frame" and never allocates them one-to-a-half and two-to-a-half. The fix is confined to the figure brief: add the same schematic qualifier FIG. 2 already carries. No application text needs to change, and nothing should be added to the description or claims to justify the visual choice.","findings":[{"severity":"minor","category":"disclosure_fidelity","title":"FIG. 1 brief states the circumferential positions of the three jaw carriages and their allocation between the frame halves as fact, without the schematic qualifier FIG. 2 uses for the same choice","where":"figures/FIG-1.md:13 (and the corresponding positions in figures/FIG-2.md:11)","detail":"The FIG. 1 brief fixes both the circumferential positions of the three jaw carriages and how many sit on each frame half. The allocation (one carriage on first frame half 10, two on second frame half 12) is a count-per-part and a relative-location assertion: it places two of the three carriages on the same segment that the wedge drives directly and one on the coupled segment. The disclosure never allocates the carriages between the halves; it says only that they are "distributed around the closed frame." A plan view must put the three carriages somewhere, so this qualifies as a depiction convention, but only if the brief marks it as one. FIG. 1 does not: the inline "shown schematically" in the same sentence governs the block depiction of the carriage, not the positions. The parallel choice in FIG. 2 is expressly marked schematic ("Shown schematically: the form of the meeting surfaces at the two joints, the positions and tilt of the three slots..."), so the two briefs label the identical choice inconsistently. The claims and description remain shape-neutral and position-neutral (claim 9 recites only that the carriages are "distributed around the frame in the closed condition such that the three jaw carriages approach the pipe received in the frame from three different directions"; draft/08-detailed-description.md:7 says the same), so no application text needs to change.","evidence":"Candidate, figures/FIG-1.md:13: "Three jaw carriages 30 are spaced around the annular frame body, at the top, the lower left and the lower right, the topmost on the first frame half 10 and the others on the second frame half 12. At each position the inner circle is interrupted by a radial opening and the jaw carriage 30 is shown schematically as a block reaching radially inward through that opening..." Nearest source passage, input/disclosure.md:5: "Three radial jaw carriages are distributed around the closed frame." There is no affirmative passage in input/disclosure.md or in the USER passage of input/conversation.md that states the circumferential positions of the carriages or how many are carried by each frame half. Contrast the label used for the same choice in figures/FIG-2.md:3: "Shown schematically: the form of the meeting surfaces at the two joints, the positions and tilt of the three slots, and the position, length, form and depth of the ring drive face 36."","fix":"In figures/FIG-1.md only, mark the placement as a depiction convention so it matches FIG. 2. Replace the first sentence of line 13 with: "Three jaw carriages 30 are spaced around the annular frame body, at the top, the lower left and the lower right, the topmost on the first frame half 10 and the others on the second frame half 12, these circumferential positions and their distribution between the two frame halves being shown schematically and chosen to correspond to the positions of the three oblique slots 34 in FIG. 2." Make no change to draft/07-drawings.md, draft/08-detailed-description.md, or the claims; do not add any statement that the carriages may be otherwise positioned or otherwise distributed."}]}
